--
-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: the parts of commencement, proclamation and appointment
-- that `bc-interpretation-time.l4` leaves out (ss 3(4), 5(2), 16(1), 16(3), 20(1), 20(2) and 20(5)). The moments at which
-- an enactment, a proclamation or an appointment starts and ends are in `bc-interpretation-time.l4`.
--
-- What FALSE and REFUSE mean here (NOTES.md, finding 2). TRUE: the case is within the provision and the provision gives the
-- thing. FALSE: only where the words of the provision give the negative themselves (an exception, "is not", "must ... one
-- whose"). REFUSE: the case is outside what the provision speaks of, or the provision only permits or "includes" and the
-- case is not listed; the text is silent and a default would be a guess.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude

§ `s 3(4) The date of assent is part of the Act`

DECLARE `A date printed with an Act` IS ONE OF
    `The date of assent`
    `The date of signification`
    `Another date`

-- src:31 | (4) The date of assent or signification is part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 3(4) (src:31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) speaks only of the date of assent and the date of signification` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 3(4) speaks only of the date of assent and the date of signification"

-- src:31 | (4) The date of assent or signification is part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 3(4) (src:31)
GIVEN date IS A `A date printed with an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) the date is part of the Act` date MEANS
    CONSIDER date
        WHEN `The date of assent` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The date of signification` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Another date` THEN `s 3(4) speaks only of the date of assent and the date of signification`

§ `s 5(2) Staggered commencement`

DECLARE `How an enactment is to come into force or be repealed` IS ONE OF
    `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
    `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
    `In some other way`

-- src:42 | (2) If an enactment is to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council,
-- src:43 | (a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of any provision of the enactment, and
-- src:44 | (b) proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times for different provisions of the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 5(2) (src:42-44)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"

-- src:42 | (2) If an enactment is to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council,
-- src:43 | (a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of any provision of the enactment, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 5(2)(a) (src:42-43)
GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment is to come into force or be repealed`
      `the provision is a provision of the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` how `the provision is a provision of the enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
        WHEN `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` THEN
            IF   `the provision is a provision of the enactment`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
        WHEN `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` THEN
            IF   `the provision is a provision of the enactment`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
        WHEN `In some other way` THEN `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`

-- src:42 | (2) If an enactment is to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council,
-- src:44 | (b) proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times for different provisions of the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 5(2)(b) (src:42, src:44)
GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment is to come into force or be repealed`
      `the provisions are different provisions of the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` how `the provisions are different provisions of the enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
        WHEN `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` THEN
            IF   `the provisions are different provisions of the enactment`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
        WHEN `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` THEN
            IF   `the provisions are different provisions of the enactment`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
        WHEN `In some other way` THEN `s 5(2) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`

§ `s 16 Proclamation`

-- src:92 | 16 (1) In a proclamation, it is not necessary to mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 16(1) (src:92)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) speaks only of a proclamation` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 16(1) speaks only of a proclamation"

-- src:92 | 16 (1) In a proclamation, it is not necessary to mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 16(1) (src:92)
GIVEN `the instrument is a proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) a proclamation must mention that it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` `the instrument is a proclamation` MEANS
    IF   `the instrument is a proclamation`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `s 16(1) speaks only of a proclamation`

-- src:94 | (3) If an enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation, judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation without being specially pleaded.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 16(3) (src:94)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation"

-- src:94 | (3) If an enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation, judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation without being specially pleaded.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 16(3) (src:94)
GIVEN `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation` `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation`

-- src:94 | (3) If an enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation, judicial notice must be taken of the issue of the proclamation without being specially pleaded.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 16(3) (src:94)
GIVEN `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the issue of the proclamation must be specially pleaded` `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment is expressed to come into force on proclamation`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `s 16(3) speaks only of an enactment expressed to come into force on proclamation`

§ `s 20 Appointments of officers`

-- "appointing instrument means an enactment that appoints a person to an office": "means" closes the definition.
-- src:120 | 20 (1) In this section, appointing instrument means an enactment that appoints a person to an office.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(1) (src:120)
GIVEN `the instrument is an enactment`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument appoints a person to an office`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) an instrument is an appointing instrument` `the instrument is an enactment` `the instrument appoints a person to an office` MEANS
    `the instrument is an enactment` AND `the instrument appoints a person to an office`

DECLARE `How long an appointment of a public officer lasts` IS ONE OF
    `During pleasure`
    `For a fixed term`
    `In some other way`

-- src:121 | (2) An authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint during pleasure.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(2) (src:121)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) speaks only of an authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 20(2) speaks only of an authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer"

-- Fork F-pleasure: the sentence names appointment "during pleasure" and does not say the authority is only for that, nor what
-- an appointment during pleasure allows. The two refusals below are the first reading; the others are asserted, to fail,
-- in `bc-tests-alt-readings-2-expected-fail.l4`.
-- src:121 | (2) An authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint during pleasure.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(2) (src:121)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that"

-- src:121 | (2) An authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint during pleasure.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(2) (src:121)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) does not say what an appointment during pleasure allows: ending it at will, without notice or without cause` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 20(2) does not say what an appointment during pleasure allows: ending it at will, without notice or without cause"

-- src:121 | (2) An authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint during pleasure.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(2) (src:121)
GIVEN how IS A `How long an appointment of a public officer lasts`
      `the authority is under an enactment to appoint a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the authority to appoint a public officer is authority to appoint in this way` how `the authority is under an enactment to appoint a public officer` MEANS
    IF   `the authority is under an enactment to appoint a public officer`
    THEN CONSIDER how
             WHEN `During pleasure` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `For a fixed term` THEN `s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that`
             WHEN `In some other way` THEN `s 20(2) names appointment during pleasure and does not say the authority is only for that`
    ELSE `s 20(2) speaks only of an authority under an enactment to appoint a public officer`

DECLARE `What section 4 is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `An appointing instrument`
    `An enactment referred to in section 20(4)(c), (d) or (e)`
    `Another enactment`

-- src:129 | (5) Section 4 [time of commencement or repeal] does not apply to an appointing instrument or an enactment referred to in subsection (4) (c), (d) or (e).
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(5) (src:129)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(5) says where section 4 does not apply and does not say it applies everywhere else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 20(5) says where section 4 does not apply and does not say it applies everywhere else"

-- src:129 | (5) Section 4 [time of commencement or repeal] does not apply to an appointing instrument or an enactment referred to in subsection (4) (c), (d) or (e).
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 20(5) (src:129)
GIVEN thing IS A `What section 4 is asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(5) section 4 applies to the instrument or enactment` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `An appointing instrument` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `An enactment referred to in section 20(4)(c), (d) or (e)` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `Another enactment` THEN `s 20(5) says where section 4 does not apply and does not say it applies everywhere else`
